# Lumen — Warp Terminal AI rules

> This file mirrors [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md). Warp Terminal's AI features (Agent Mode, suggestions) reference this when working in repos that use Lumen.

## Identity

This is the design system for **Warp** (wearewarp.com — the freight network). Not to be confused with Warp Terminal. The accent green here is the freight Warp's brand green.

## Hard rules

(Same as AGENTS.md and `.cursor/rules/lumen.mdc`. The full text lives in AGENTS.md — this file is the Warp-Terminal-friendly mirror.)

1. Use semantic Lumen tokens, never primitives.
2. Never hardcode hex / px in component code.
3. Component contracts must validate against the schema.
4. WCAG 2.2 AA hard floor.
5. Warp green = action/live/success only.
6. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Common terminal commands

```bash
pnpm install                    # install deps
pnpm build                      # build tokens (Style Dictionary)
pnpm validate                   # JSON schema + DTCG lint + WCAG
pnpm registry                   # regenerate _registry/
cd audit-dashboard && pnpm dev  # run reference dashboard
```

## Quick lookups

When you need to reference a Lumen value, query in this order:
1. `_registry/{name}.json` — installable component metadata
2. `design-system/02-components/{name}/component.json` — full contract
3. `design-system/01-tokens/semantic/*.tokens.json` — tokens
4. `design-system/01-tokens/README.md` — token taxonomy & quick-ref tables
